<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Megiddo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1457 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century-bce">15th century BCE</a> · Also known as Megiddo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Megiddo, dated by the site to 1457 BCE, was fought in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> and a coalition of Canaanite rulers led by the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a>. The Egyptian victory, followed by a siege of Megiddo, is one of the earliest battles recorded in detail. It established Egyptian dominance over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> in the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>.</p></div>
